T* (## 1\) Executive summary) Tj
T* (Australia has a **federal, multi-level political finance system**. There is no single Australian) Tj
T* (campaign finance code. Instead, obligations vary by election type and jurisdiction. Core regulatory) Tj
T* (levers are:) Tj
T* (- disclosure/reporting of donations and electoral expenditure) Tj
T* (- caps on donations and/or expenditure \(in some jurisdictions\)) Tj
T* (- source restrictions \(especially foreign donations; and sectoral bans in some states\)) Tj
T* (- public funding mechanisms) Tj
T* (- compliance/audit/enforcement powers.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (As of this review date, a major national reform package \(Electoral Reform Act 2025\) is implementing) Tj
T* (significant Commonwealth changes from **1 July 2026**, including lower disclosure thresholds and faster) Tj
T* (disclosure in election periods.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 2\) Constitutional and institutional context) Tj
T* (- **Commonwealth:** regulated primarily under the *Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918* \(Part XX and related) Tj
T* (provisions\), administered by the Australian Electoral Commission \(AEC\).) Tj
T* (- **States/territories:** each has separate electoral finance statutes and regulators.) Tj
T* (- **Local government:** usually regulated by **state/territory law**, either in the same) Tj
T* (funding/disclosure statute used for state elections or via dedicated local-government election) Tj
T* (legislation.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 3\) Commonwealth \(federal\) rules) Tj
T* (### 3.1 Core law and administrator) Tj
T* (- *Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918*.) Tj
T* (- AEC Funding and Disclosure framework.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### 3.2 Key architecture) Tj
T* (Historically, Commonwealth law has emphasized disclosure and public funding, with tighter controls added) Tj
T* (progressively \(including foreign-donation controls and regulation of third-party political campaigners\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### 3.3 Current reform phase \(critical\)) Tj
