T* (## 4\) State and territory frameworks) Tj
T* (> Important: rules differ substantially, and some thresholds/caps are indexed or changed by periodic) Tj
T* (notices.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### New South Wales \(NSW\)) Tj
T* (- Primary law: *Electoral Funding Act 2018 \(NSW\)*.) Tj
T* (- Features: donation caps, expenditure caps, disclosure framework, and application to state and local) Tj
T* (election participants under NSWs scheme.) Tj
T* (- Regulator: NSW Electoral Commission.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### Victoria \(VIC\)) Tj
T* (- Primary law: *Electoral Act 2002 \(Vic\)* \(Part 12 and related amendments\).) Tj
T* (- Features: caps/disclosure framework for state elections; foreign-donation restrictions; anti-avoidance) Tj
T* (provisions.) Tj
T* (- Local-council donation regulation is administered separately \(via local government integrity) Tj
T* (architecture\), even though state-level rules are in the Electoral Act.) Tj
T* (- Regulator: Victorian Electoral Commission \(state-level disclosures\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### Queensland \(QLD\)) Tj
T* (- Primary laws: *Electoral Act 1992 \(Qld\)* and *Local Government Electoral Act 2011 \(Qld\)*.) Tj
T* (- Features: disclosure regime for political donations/expenditure, donation caps, expenditure caps, and) Tj
T* (restrictions affecting certain donor classes.) Tj
T* (- Regulator: Electoral Commission of Queensland.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### Western Australia \(WA\)) Tj
T* (- Primary law: *Electoral Act 1907 \(WA\)* \(as amended, including 2023 reforms\) plus regulations.) Tj
T* (- Features: enhanced disclosure and political finance controls from July 2024 reforms, including foreign) Tj
T* (donation settings and spending/disclosure controls.) Tj
T* (- Regulator: WA Electoral Commission.) Tj
T* (- Local-government gift rules also operate under WA local-government election framework.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### South Australia \(SA\)) Tj
T* (- Primary law: *Electoral Act 1985 \(SA\)* \(notably amended by the *Electoral \(Accountability and) Tj
T* (Integrity\) Amendment Act 2024*\).) Tj
T* (- Features: SA has moved to one of the strongest interventionist models, with broad donation) Tj
T* (prohibitions and tightly structured exceptions/controls \(including treatment of new entrants and third) Tj
T* (parties under caps/reporting rules\).) Tj
