T* (- Primary law: *Electoral Act 2004 \(NT\)*.) Tj
T* (- Features: Part 10 framework for donations, expenditure and disclosure; reporting obligations for) Tj
T* (parties/candidates/donors and election-period controls.) Tj
T* (- Regulator: Northern Territory Electoral Commission.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 5\) Local-government level) Tj
T* (There is no uniform national local-government campaign finance code. In practice:) Tj
T* (- NSW and QLD: local election participants are directly integrated into state electoral) Tj
T* (finance/disclosure systems.) Tj
T* (- WA and others: local-government-specific gift/disclosure rules coexist with broader state electoral) Tj
T* (finance law.) Tj
T* (- Victoria: local-council candidate donations involve separate administration pathways from state) Tj
T* (election disclosures.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (**Practical implication:** compliance must be mapped election-by-election \(state lower house, upper) Tj
T* (house, council, mayoral, by-election\), because definitions of gift, political donation, aggregation,) Tj
T* (return timing, and enforcement differ.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 6\) Major reforms over time \(high-level timeline\)) Tj
T* (- **1980s \(Commonwealth\):** public funding and modern disclosure architecture introduced.) Tj
T* (- **2000s \(Commonwealth\):** higher disclosure thresholds with indexation became a central controversy.) Tj
T* (- **2018 \(Commonwealth\):** *Electoral Legislation Amendment \(Electoral Funding and Disclosure Reform\)) Tj
T* (Act 2018* tightened foreign-donation and third-party campaigner regulation.) Tj
T* (- **20232025 \(states\):** substantial state-level redesigns \(e.g., WA amendments effective 2024; SAs) Tj
T* (major 2024 amending Act effective from 2025 settings\).) Tj
T* (- **20252026 \(Commonwealth\):** *Electoral Reform Act 2025* rollout from 1 July 2026, including lower) Tj
T* (threshold and faster disclosure.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## 7\) Key policy debates) Tj
T* (1. **Transparency timing:** annual disclosure vs near-real-time reporting.) Tj
T* (2. **Donation caps vs free political communication:** constitutional proportionality and implied freedom) Tj
T* (issues.) Tj
T* (3. **Third-party regulation:** balancing anti-circumvention with civil society participation.) Tj
T* (4. **Foreign influence controls:** broad consensus on restrictions, disagreement on scope and) Tj
